#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Definition of purifications {#definition-of-purifications}"
msgstr "Takrifan penulenan {#definition-of-purifications}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let us begin with a precise mathematical definition for purifications.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita mulakan dengan takrifan matematik yang tepat bagi penulenan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Definition\">\n"
"Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system in a state represented by a density matrix $\\rho,$ and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a quantum state vector of a pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that leaves $\\rho$ when $\\mathsf{Y}$ is traced out:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
"The state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is then said to be a *purification* of $\\rho.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Takrifan\">\n"
"Andaikan $\\mathsf{X}$ ialah sistem dalam keadaan yang diwakili oleh matriks ketumpatan $\\rho,$ dan $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ialah vektor keadaan kuantum bagi pasangan $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ yang meninggalkan $\\rho$ apabila $\\mathsf{Y}$ disurih keluar:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
"Vektor keadaan $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ kemudiannya dikatakan sebagai sebuah *penulenan* bagi $\\rho.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The pure state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert,$ expressed as a "
"density matrix rather than a quantum state vector, is also commonly referred"
" to as a purification of $\\rho$ when the equation in the definition is "
"true, but we'll generally use the term to refer to a quantum state vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Keadaan tulen $\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert,$ yang dinyatakan "
"sebagai matriks ketumpatan dan bukannya vektor keadaan kuantum, juga "
"lazimnya dirujuk sebagai penulenan bagi $\\rho$ apabila persamaan dalam "
"takrifan itu benar, tetapi kita umumnya akan menggunakan istilah tersebut "
"untuk merujuk kepada vektor keadaan kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The term *purification* is also used more generally when the ordering of the systems is reversed, when the names of the systems and states are different (of course), and when there are more than two systems.\n"
"For instance, if $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ is a quantum state vector representing a pure state of a compound system $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ and the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Istilah *penulenan* juga digunakan secara lebih umum apabila urutan sistem dibalikkan, apabila nama-nama sistem dan keadaan berbeza (sudah tentu), dan apabila terdapat lebih daripada dua sistem.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, jika $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ ialah vektor keadaan kuantum yang mewakili keadaan tulen sistem kompaun $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ dan persamaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is true for a density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of the system "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{C}),$ then $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is still referred to"
" as a purification of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"benar bagi matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ yang mewakili keadaan sistem "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{C}),$ maka $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ masih dirujuk "
"sebagai penulenan bagi $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the purposes of this lesson, however, we'll focus on the specific form described in the definition.\n"
"Properties and facts concerning purifications, according to this definition, can typically be generalized to more than two systems by re-ordering and partitioning the systems into two compound systems, one playing the role of $\\mathsf{X}$ and the other playing the role of $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Walau bagaimanapun, untuk tujuan pelajaran ini, kita akan fokus pada bentuk khusus yang diterangkan dalam takrifan tersebut.\n"
"Sifat-sifat dan fakta-fakta mengenai penulenan, mengikut takrifan ini, biasanya boleh diumumkan kepada lebih daripada dua sistem dengan mengatur semula dan membahagikan sistem kepada dua sistem kompaun, satu memainkan peranan $\\mathsf{X}$ dan satu lagi memainkan peranan $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Existence of purifications {#existence-of-purifications}"
msgstr "Kewujudan penulenan {#existence-of-purifications}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are any two systems and $\\rho$ is a given state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"We will prove that there exists a quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that *purifies* $\\rho$ — which is another way of saying that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a purification of $\\rho$ — provided that the system $\\mathsf{Y}$ is large enough.\n"
"In particular, if $\\mathsf{Y}$ has at least as many classical states as $\\mathsf{X},$ then a purification of this form necessarily exists for every state $\\rho.$\n"
"Fewer classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ are required for some states $\\rho;$\n"
"in general, $\\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ are necessary and sufficient for the existence of a quantum state vector of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that purifies $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Andaikan $\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ adalah dua sistem sewenang-wenangnya dan $\\rho$ ialah keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ yang diberikan.\n"
"Kita akan membuktikan bahawa terdapat vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ bagi $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ yang *menulenkan* $\\rho$ — iaitu satu cara lain menyatakan bahawa $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ adalah penulenan bagi $\\rho$ — dengan syarat sistem $\\mathsf{Y}$ cukup besar.\n"
"Khususnya, jika $\\mathsf{Y}$ mempunyai sekurang-kurangnya bilangan keadaan klasik yang sama seperti $\\mathsf{X},$ maka penulenan berbentuk ini semestinya wujud bagi setiap keadaan $\\rho.$\n"
"Bilangan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{Y}$ yang lebih sedikit diperlukan untuk sesetengah keadaan $\\rho;$\n"
"secara umum, $\\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{Y}$ adalah perlu dan mencukupi untuk kewujudan vektor keadaan kuantum $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ yang menulenkan $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider first any expression of $\\rho$ as a convex combination of $n$ pure"
" states, for any positive integer $n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan dahulu sebarang ungkapan $\\rho$ sebagai kombinasi cembung $n$"
" keadaan tulen, bagi sebarang integer positif $n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this expression, $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ is a probability vector and "
"$\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ are quantum state "
"vectors of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam ungkapan ini, $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ ialah vektor kebarangkalian dan "
"$\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ ialah vektor-"
"vektor keadaan kuantum $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to obtain such an expression is through the spectral theorem, in "
"which case $n$ is the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X},$ "
"$p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ are the eigenvalues of $\\rho,$ and "
"$\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ are orthonormal "
"eigenvectors corresponding to these eigenvalues.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu cara untuk mendapatkan ungkapan sedemikian ialah melalui teorem "
"spektrum, dalam kes itu $n$ ialah bilangan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X},$ "
"$p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ adalah nilai eigen $\\rho,$ dan "
"$\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ adalah vektor-"
"vektor eigen ortonormal yang sepadan dengan nilai-nilai eigen ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's actually no need to include the terms corresponding to the zero eigenvalues of $\\rho$ in the sum, which allows us to alternatively choose $n = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ and $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ to be the non-zero eigenvalues of $\\rho.$\n"
"This is the minimum value of $n$ for which an expression of $\\rho$ taking the form above exists.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebenarnya tidak perlu memasukkan sebutan-sebutan yang sepadan dengan nilai eigen sifar $\\rho$ dalam jumlah itu, yang membolehkan kita secara alternatif memilih $n = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ dan $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ sebagai nilai-nilai eigen bukan sifar $\\rho.$\n"
"Ini adalah nilai minimum $n$ di mana ungkapan $\\rho$ yang mengambil bentuk di atas wujud.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, it is *not necessary* that the chosen expression of $\\rho,$ as a convex combination of pure states, comes from the spectral theorem — this is just one way to obtain such an expression.\n"
"In particular, $n$ could be any positive integer, the unit vectors $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ need not be orthogonal, and the probabilities $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ need not be eigenvalues of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menjelaskan, *tidak perlu* bahawa ungkapan $\\rho$ yang dipilih, sebagai kombinasi cembung keadaan tulen, berasal dari teorem spektrum — ini hanyalah satu cara untuk mendapatkan ungkapan sedemikian.\n"
"Khususnya, $n$ boleh menjadi sebarang integer positif, vektor-vektor unit $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ tidak perlu ortogon, dan kebarangkalian $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ tidak perlu menjadi nilai eigen $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can now identify a purification of $\\rho$ as follows.\n"
msgstr "Kita kini boleh mengenal pasti penulenan $\\rho$ seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're making the assumption that the classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ include $0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
"If they do not, an arbitrary choice for $n$ distinct classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ can be substituted for $0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
"Verifying that this is indeed a purification of $\\rho$ is a simple matter of computing the partial trace, which can be done in the following two equivalent ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita membuat andaian bahawa keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{Y}$ merangkumi $0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
"Jika tidak, pilihan sewenang-wenang bagi $n$ keadaan klasik berbeza $\\mathsf{Y}$ boleh digantikan dengan $0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
"Mengesahkan bahawa ini memang penulenan bagi $\\rho$ adalah perkara mudah untuk mengira surih separa, yang boleh dilakukan dalam dua cara setara berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\langle a\\vert) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\langle a\\vert) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_b\\vert\n"
"\\, \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert a \\rangle \\langle b \\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_b\\vert\n"
"\\, \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert a \\rangle \\langle b \\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More generally, for any orthonormal set of vectors "
"$\\{\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{n-1}\\rangle\\},$ the "
"quantum state vector\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih umum lagi, bagi sebarang set ortonormal vektor "
"$\\{\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{n-1}\\rangle\\},$ vektor "
"keadaan kuantum\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is a purification of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr "adalah penulenan bagi $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example {#example}"
msgstr "Contoh {#example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are both qubits and\n"
msgstr "Andaikan $\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ keduanya adalah qubit dan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is a density matrix representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr "adalah matriks ketumpatan yang mewakili keadaan $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can use the spectral theorem to express $\\rho$ as\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh menggunakan teorem spektrum untuk menyatakan $\\rho$ sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle = \\cos(\\theta) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta)\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"The quantum state vector\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle = \\cos(\\theta) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta)\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Vektor keadaan kuantum\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\sin(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\sin(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which describes a pure state of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}),$ is "
"therefore a purification of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"yang menggambarkan keadaan tulen pasangan $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}),$ oleh "
"itu merupakan penulenan bagi $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, we can write\n"
msgstr "Secara alternatif, kita boleh menulis\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a convex combination of pure states but not a spectral decomposition because $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert +\\rangle$ are not orthogonal and $1/2$ is not an eigenvalue of $\\rho.$\n"
"Nevertheless, the quantum state vector\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah kombinasi cembung keadaan-keadaan tulen tetapi bukan penguraian spektrum kerana $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert +\\rangle$ tidak ortogon dan $1/2$ bukan nilai eigen $\\rho.$\n"
"Walaupun begitu, vektor keadaan kuantum\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Schmidt decompositions {#schmidt-decompositions}"
msgstr "Penguraian Schmidt {#schmidt-decompositions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we will discuss *Schmidt decompositions*, which are expressions of quantum state vectors of *pairs* of systems that take a certain form.\n"
"Schmidt decompositions are closely connected with purifications, and they're very useful in their own right.\n"
"Indeed, when reasoning about a given quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ of a pair of systems, the first step is often to identify or consider a Schmidt decomposition of this state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, kita akan membincangkan *penguraian Schmidt*, iaitu ungkapan-ungkapan vektor keadaan kuantum bagi *pasangan* sistem yang mengambil bentuk tertentu.\n"
"Penguraian Schmidt berkaitan rapat dengan penulenan, dan ia sangat berguna dalam haknya sendiri.\n"
"Memang, apabila membuat alasan tentang vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ yang diberikan bagi sepasang sistem, langkah pertama sering kali adalah mengenal pasti atau mempertimbangkan penguraian Schmidt bagi keadaan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Definition\">\n"
"Let $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ be a given quantum state vector of a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$ A *Schmidt decomposition* of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an expression of the form\n"
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
"where $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ are positive real numbers summing to $1$ and *both* of the sets $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ and $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are orthonormal.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Takrifan\">\n"
"Biar $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ ialah vektor keadaan kuantum yang diberikan bagi sepasang sistem $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$ Sebuah *penguraian Schmidt* bagi $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ialah ungkapan berbentuk\n"
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
"di mana $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ adalah nombor nyata positif yang berjumlah kepada $1$ dan *kedua-dua* set $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ dan $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ adalah ortonormal.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The values\n"
msgstr "Nilai-nilai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{p_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{p_{r-1}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{p_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{p_{r-1}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"in a Schmidt decomposition of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ are known as its *Schmidt coefficients*, which are uniquely determined (up to their ordering) — they're the only positive real numbers that can appear in such an expression of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"The sets\n"
msgstr ""
"dalam penguraian Schmidt bagi $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ dikenali sebagai *pekali Schmidt*-nya, yang ditentukan secara unik (sehingga tertib mereka) — ia adalah satu-satunya nombor nyata positif yang boleh muncul dalam ungkapan sedemikian bagi $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Set-set\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\} \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\} \\quad\\text{dan}\\quad\n"
"\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"on the other hand, are not uniquely determined, and the freedom one has in "
"choosing these sets of vectors will be clarified in the explanation that "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"sebaliknya, tidak ditentukan secara unik, dan kebebasan yang ada dalam "
"memilih set-set vektor ini akan dijelaskan dalam huraian yang berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll now verify that a given quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ "
"does indeed have a Schmidt decomposition, and in the process, we'll learn "
"how to find one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini akan mengesahkan bahawa vektor keadaan kuantum "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ yang diberikan memang mempunyai penguraian Schmidt, "
"dan dalam proses itu, kita akan mempelajari cara mencarinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider first an arbitrary (not necessarily orthogonal) basis $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ of the vector space corresponding to the system $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Because this is a basis, there will always exist a uniquely determined selection of vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ for which the following equation is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan dahulu asas yang sewenang-wenang (tidak semestinya ortogon) $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ bagi ruang vektor yang sepadan dengan sistem $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Kerana ini adalah asas, akan sentiasa wujud pemilihan vektor $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ yang ditentukan secara unik di mana persamaan berikut benar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a \\rangle\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a \\rangle\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, suppose $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is the standard basis associated with $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Assuming the classical state set of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ this means that $\\vert x_a\\rangle = \\vert a\\rangle$ for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ and we find that\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, andaikan $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ialah asas piawai yang dikaitkan dengan $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Dengan menganggap set keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$ ialah $\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ ini bermakna $\\vert x_a\\rangle = \\vert a\\rangle$ bagi setiap $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ dan kita mendapati bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "when\n"
msgstr "apabila\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = ( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = ( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}.$\n"
"We frequently consider expressions like this when contemplating a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"bagi setiap $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}.$\n"
"Kita kerap mempertimbangkan ungkapan seperti ini apabila memikirkan tentang pengukuran asas piawai $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It's important to note that the formula\n"
msgstr "Penting untuk diingat bahawa formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for the vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ in this example only works because $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert n-1\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal* basis.\n"
"In general, if $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is a basis that is not necessarily orthonormal, then the vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ are still uniquely determined by the equation $(1),$ but a different formula is needed.\n"
"One way to find them is first to identify vectors $\\vert w_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert w_{n-1}\\rangle$ so that the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"bagi vektor-vektor $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ dalam contoh ini hanya berfungsi kerana $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert n-1\\rangle\\}$ adalah asas *ortonormal*.\n"
"Secara umum, jika $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ialah asas yang tidak semestinya ortonormal, maka vektor-vektor $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ masih ditentukan secara unik oleh persamaan $(1),$ tetapi formula yang berbeza diperlukan.\n"
"Satu cara untuk mencarinya ialah dengan terlebih dahulu mengenal pasti vektor-vektor $\\vert w_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert w_{n-1}\\rangle$ supaya persamaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle w_a \\vert x_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases} 1 & a=b\\\\ 0 & a\\neq b \\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle w_a \\vert x_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases} 1 & a=b\\\\ 0 & a\\neq b \\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is satisfied for all $a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ at which point we have\n"
msgstr ""
"dipenuhi bagi semua $a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ pada ketika itu kita "
"mempunyai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = (\\langle w_a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = (\\langle w_a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a given basis $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ of the vector space corresponding to $\\mathsf{X},$ the uniquely determined vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ for which the equation $(1)$ is satisfied won't necessarily satisfy any special properties, even if $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ happens to be an orthonormal basis.\n"
"If, however, we choose $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ to be an orthonormal basis of *eigenvectors* of the reduced state\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagi asas $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ yang diberikan bagi ruang vektor yang sepadan dengan $\\mathsf{X},$ vektor-vektor yang ditentukan secara unik $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ di mana persamaan $(1)$ dipenuhi tidak semestinya memenuhi sebarang sifat khas, walaupun jika $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ kebetulan adalah asas ortonormal.\n"
"Namun, jika kita memilih $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ sebagai asas ortonormal *vektor eigen* bagi keadaan teraruh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"then something interesting happens.\n"
"Specifically, for the uniquely determined collection $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ for which the equation $(1)$ is true, we find that this collection must be *orthogonal.*\n"
msgstr ""
"maka sesuatu yang menarik berlaku.\n"
"Khususnya, bagi koleksi $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ yang ditentukan secara unik di mana persamaan $(1)$ benar, kita mendapati bahawa koleksi ini mestilah *ortogon.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In greater detail, consider a spectral decomposition of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr "Dengan lebih terperinci, pertimbangkan penguraian spektrum $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're denoting the eigenvalues of $\\rho$ by $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ in recognition of the fact that $\\rho$ is a density matrix — so the vector of eigenvalues $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ forms a probability vector — while $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of eigenvectors corresponding to these eigenvalues.\n"
"To see that the unique collection $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ for which the equation $(1)$ is true is necessarily orthogonal, we can begin by computing the partial trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita menandakan nilai-nilai eigen $\\rho$ dengan $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ sebagai pengiktirafan fakta bahawa $\\rho$ adalah matriks ketumpatan — jadi vektor nilai eigen $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ membentuk vektor kebarangkalian — manakala $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ialah asas ortonormal vektor-vektor eigen yang sepadan dengan nilai-nilai eigen ini.\n"
"Untuk melihat bahawa koleksi unik $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ di mana persamaan $(1)$ benar semestinya ortogon, kita boleh mulakan dengan mengira surih separa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert z_a\\rangle\\langle z_b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\langle z_b\\vert z_a\\rangle \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert z_a\\rangle\\langle z_b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\langle z_b\\vert z_a\\rangle \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This expression must agree with the spectral decomposition of $\\rho.$\n"
"Because $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is a basis, we conclude that the set of matrices\n"
msgstr ""
"Ungkapan ini mestilah bersetuju dengan penguraian spektrum $\\rho.$\n"
"Kerana $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ialah asas, kita menyimpulkan bahawa set matriks\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\,:\\, a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\,:\\, a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is linearly independent, and so it follows that\n"
msgstr "adalah bebas linear, dan oleh itu ia mengikut bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle z_b \\vert z_a\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  p_a & a=b\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & a\\neq b,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle z_b \\vert z_a\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  p_a & a=b\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & a\\neq b,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"establishing that $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ "
"is orthogonal.\n"
msgstr ""
"membuktikan bahawa $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$"
" adalah ortogon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've nearly obtained a Schmidt decomposition of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"It remains to discard those terms in $(1)$ for which $p_a = 0$ and then write $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ for a unit vector $\\vert y_a\\rangle$ for each of the remaining terms.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita hampir mendapat penguraian Schmidt bagi $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Tinggal lagi untuk membuang sebutan-sebutan dalam $(1)$ di mana $p_a = 0$ kemudian menulis $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ bagi vektor unit $\\vert y_a\\rangle$ bagi setiap sebutan yang tinggal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A convenient way to do this begins with the observation that we're free to "
"number the eigenvalue/eigenvector pairs in a spectral decomposition of the "
"reduced state $\\rho$ however we wish — so we may assume that the "
"eigenvalues are sorted in decreasing order:\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu cara yang mudah untuk melakukan ini bermula dengan pemerhatian bahawa "
"kita bebas untuk menomborkan pasangan nilai eigen/vektor eigen dalam "
"penguraian spektrum keadaan teraruh $\\rho$ sesuka hati — jadi kita boleh "
"menganggap nilai-nilai eigen tersusun dalam tertib menurun:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p_0 \\geq p_1 \\geq \\cdots \\geq p_{n-1}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p_0 \\geq p_1 \\geq \\cdots \\geq p_{n-1}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Letting $r = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho),$ we find that $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1} > 0$ and $p_r = \\cdots = p_{n-1} = 0.$\n"
"So, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan menetapkan $r = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho),$ kita mendapati bahawa $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1} > 0$ dan $p_r = \\cdots = p_{n-1} = 0.$\n"
"Jadi, kita mempunyai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and we can write the quantum state vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ as\n"
msgstr ""
"dan kita boleh menulis vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ "
"sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Given that\n"
msgstr "Memandangkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\| \\vert z_a \\rangle \\|^2 = \\langle z_a \\vert z_a \\rangle = p_a > 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\| \\vert z_a \\rangle \\|^2 = \\langle z_a \\vert z_a \\rangle = p_a > 0\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for $a=0,\\ldots,r-1,$ we can define unit vectors $\\vert y_0 "
"\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle$ as\n"
msgstr ""
"bagi $a=0,\\ldots,r-1,$ kita boleh mentakrifkan vektor-vektor unit $\\vert "
"y_0 \\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle$ sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert y_a\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\|\\vert z_a\\rangle\\|} = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\sqrt{p_a}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert y_a\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\|\\vert z_a\\rangle\\|} = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\sqrt{p_a}},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"so that $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,r-1\\}.$\n"
"Because the vectors $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert z_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are orthogonal and nonzero, it follows that\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal* set, and so we have obtained a Schmidt decomposition of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"supaya $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ bagi setiap $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,r-1\\}.$\n"
"Kerana vektor-vektor $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert z_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ adalah ortogon dan bukan sifar, ia mengikut bahawa\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ adalah set *ortonormal*, dan kita telah mendapat penguraian Schmidt bagi $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Concerning the choice of the vectors\n"
"$\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},$\n"
"we can select $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ to be any orthonormal set of eigenvectors corresponding to the nonzero eigenvalues of the reduced state $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ (as we have done above), in which case the vectors $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are uniquely determined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengenai pilihan vektor-vektor\n"
"$\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ dan\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},$\n"
"kita boleh memilih $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ sebagai sebarang set ortonormal vektor eigen yang sepadan dengan nilai-nilai eigen bukan sifar keadaan teraruh $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ (seperti yang kita lakukan di atas), dalam kes itu vektor-vektor $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ditentukan secara unik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The situation is symmetric between the two systems, so we can alternatively "
"choose $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ to be any "
"orthonormal set of eigenvectors corresponding to the nonzero eigenvalues of "
"the reduced state "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert),$ "
"in which case the vectors $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ will be uniquely determined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Situasinya adalah simetri antara kedua-dua sistem, jadi kita boleh secara "
"alternatif memilih $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$"
" sebagai sebarang set ortonormal vektor eigen yang sepadan dengan nilai-"
"nilai eigen bukan sifar keadaan teraruh "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert),$ "
"dalam kes itu vektor-vektor $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ akan ditentukan secara unik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice, however, that once one of the sets is selected, as a set of "
"eigenvectors of the corresponding reduced state as just described, the other"
" is determined — so they cannot be chosen independently.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perlu diingat, bagaimanapun, bahawa setelah satu set dipilih, sebagai "
"vektor-vektor eigen keadaan teraruh yang sepadan seperti yang baru "
"diterangkan, yang satu lagi ditentukan — jadi ia tidak boleh dipilih secara "
"bebas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Although it won't come up again in this series, it is noteworthy that the "
"non-zero eigenvalues $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ of the reduced state "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ "
"must always agree with the nonzero eigenvalues of the reduced state "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ "
"for any pure state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ of a pair of systems "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun tidak akan timbul lagi dalam siri ini, adalah penting untuk "
"diperhatikan bahawa nilai-nilai eigen bukan sifar $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ bagi"
" keadaan teraruh "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ "
"mestilah sentiasa bersetuju dengan nilai-nilai eigen bukan sifar keadaan "
"teraruh "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ "
"bagi mana-mana keadaan tulen $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ sepasang sistem "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, the reduced states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ have exactly the same amount of randomness in them when the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is in a pure state.\n"
"This fact is revealed by the Schmidt decomposition: in both cases the eigenvalues of the reduced states must agree with the squares of the Schmidt coefficients of the pure state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara intuitif, keadaan-keadaan teraruh $\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ mempunyai jumlah kerawakan yang tepat sama apabila pasangan $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ berada dalam keadaan tulen.\n"
"Fakta ini didedahkan oleh penguraian Schmidt: dalam kedua-dua kes nilai eigen keadaan teraruh mestilah bersetuju dengan kuasa dua pekali-pekali Schmidt bagi keadaan tulen.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unitary equivalence of purifications {#unitary-equivalence-of-purifications}"
msgstr "Kesetaraan unitari penulenan {#unitary-equivalence-of-purifications}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can use Schmidt decompositions to establish a fundamentally important "
"fact concerning purifications known as the *unitary equivalence of "
"purifications*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh menggunakan penguraian Schmidt untuk menetapkan fakta yang sangat"
" penting berkaitan penulenan yang dikenali sebagai *kesetaraan unitari "
"penulenan*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Unitary equivalence of purifications: Suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are systems, and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ are quantum state vectors of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that both purify the same state of $\\mathsf{X}.$ In symbols,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"
"for some density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"There must then exist a unitary operation $U$ on $\\mathsf{Y}$ alone that transforms the first purification into the second:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\phi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teorem\">\n"
"Kesetaraan unitari penulenan: Andaikan $\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ ialah sistem, dan $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ serta $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ ialah vektor keadaan kuantum bagi $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ yang kedua-duanya menulenkan keadaan yang sama bagi $\\mathsf{X}.$ Dalam simbol,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"
"untuk sesetengah matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ yang mewakili keadaan $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Mesti terdapat operasi unitari $U$ pada $\\mathsf{Y}$ sahaja yang mengubah penulenan pertama kepada yang kedua:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\phi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll discuss a few implications of this theorem as the lesson continues, "
"but first let's see how it follows from our previous discussion of Schmidt "
"decompositions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan bincangkan beberapa implikasi teorem ini semasa pelajaran "
"diteruskan, tetapi mula-mula mari kita lihat bagaimana ia mengikut daripada "
"perbincangan kita sebelum ini tentang penguraian Schmidt.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our assumption is that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ are quantum state vectors\n"
"of a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that satisfy the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Andaian kita ialah $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ dan $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ ialah vektor keadaan kuantum\n"
"bagi pasangan sistem $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ yang memenuhi persamaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for some density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk sesetengah matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ yang mewakili keadaan "
"$\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Consider a spectral decomposition of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan penguraian spektrum $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of eigenvectors of $\\rho.$\n"
"By following the prescription described previously we can obtain Schmidt decompositions for both $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ having the following form.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ialah asas ortonormal vektor eigen $\\rho.$\n"
"Dengan mengikuti preskripsi yang diterangkan sebelumnya, kita boleh mendapatkan penguraian Schmidt untuk kedua-dua $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ dan $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ yang mempunyai bentuk berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\phi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\phi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In these expressions $r$ is the rank of $\\rho$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are orthonormal sets of vectors in the space corresponding to $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam ungkapan ini $r$ ialah pangkat $\\rho$ dan\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ dan\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ialah set vektor ortonormal dalam ruang yang berpadanan dengan $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For any two orthonormal sets in the same space that have the same number of elements, there's always a unitary matrix that transforms the first set into the second, so we can choose a unitary matrix $U$ so that $U \\vert u_a\\rangle = \\vert v_a\\rangle$ for $a = 0,\\ldots,r-1.$\n"
"In particular, to find such a matrix $U$ we can first use the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process to extend our orthonormal sets to orthonormal bases\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{m-1}\\rangle\\},$ where $m$ is the dimension of the space corresponding to $\\mathsf{Y},$ and then take\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mana-mana dua set ortonormal dalam ruang yang sama yang mempunyai bilangan elemen yang sama, sentiasa terdapat matriks unitari yang mengubah set pertama kepada yang kedua, jadi kita boleh pilih matriks unitari $U$ supaya $U \\vert u_a\\rangle = \\vert v_a\\rangle$ untuk $a = 0,\\ldots,r-1.$\n"
"Khususnya, untuk mencari matriks $U$ sedemikian, kita boleh mula-mula menggunakan proses orthogonalisasi Gram-Schmidt untuk meluaskan set ortonormal kita kepada asas ortonormal\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$ dan\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{m-1}\\rangle\\},$ di mana $m$ ialah dimensi ruang yang berpadanan dengan $\\mathsf{Y},$ dan kemudian ambil\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert v_a\\rangle\\langle u_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert v_a\\rangle\\langle u_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We now find that\n"
msgstr "Kita kemudiannya dapati bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes U \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes U \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which completes the proof.\n"
msgstr "yang melengkapkan buktinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here are just a few of many interesting examples and implications connected with the unitary equivalence of purifications.\n"
"We'll see another critically important one later in the lesson, in the context of fidelity, known as *Uhlmann's theorem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah beberapa daripada banyak contoh dan implikasi menarik yang berkaitan dengan kesetaraan unitari penulenan.\n"
"Kita akan melihat satu lagi yang sangat penting kemudian dalam pelajaran, dalam konteks fideliti, yang dikenali sebagai *teorem Uhlmann*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding {#superdense-coding}"
msgstr "Pengekodan suprapadat {#superdense-coding}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the superdense coding protocol, Alice and Bob share an e-bit, meaning that Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is in the $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle$ Bell state.\n"
"The protocol describes how Alice can transform this shared state into any one of the four Bell states, $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle,$ and\n"
"$\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle,$ by applying a unitary operation to her qubit $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
"Once she has done this, she sends $\\mathsf{A}$ to Bob, and then Bob performs a measurement on the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ to see which Bell state he holds.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam protokol pengekodan suprapadat, Alice dan Bob berkongsi satu e-bit, bermakna Alice memegang qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob memegang qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ dan bersama-sama pasangan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ berada dalam keadaan Bell $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle.$\n"
"Protokol ini menerangkan bagaimana Alice boleh mengubah keadaan dikongsi ini kepada mana-mana satu daripada empat keadaan Bell, $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle,$ dan\n"
"$\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle,$ dengan menerapkan operasi unitari pada qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ miliknya.\n"
"Setelah melakukan ini, dia menghantar $\\mathsf{A}$ kepada Bob, dan kemudian Bob melakukan pengukuran pada pasangan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ untuk melihat keadaan Bell mana yang dia pegang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For all four Bell states, the reduced state of Bob's qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ is "
"the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk keempat-empat keadaan Bell, keadaan terturun qubit Bob $\\mathsf{B}$ "
"ialah keadaan bercampur penuh.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle\\langle\\phi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle\\langle\\phi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle\\langle\\psi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\frac{\\mathbb{I}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle\\langle\\phi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle\\langle\\phi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle\\langle\\psi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\frac{\\mathbb{I}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the unitary equivalence of purifications, we immediately conclude that for each Bell state there must exist a unitary operation on Alice's qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ alone that transforms $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ into the chosen Bell state.\n"
"Although this does not reveal the precise details of the protocol, the unitary equivalence of purifications does immediately imply that superdense coding is possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan kesetaraan unitari penulenan, kita segera simpulkan bahawa untuk setiap keadaan Bell mesti terdapat operasi unitari pada qubit Alice $\\mathsf{A}$ sahaja yang mengubah $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ kepada keadaan Bell yang dipilih.\n"
"Walaupun ini tidak mendedahkan butiran tepat protokol tersebut, kesetaraan unitari penulenan memang segera menunjukkan bahawa pengekodan suprapadat adalah mungkin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also conclude that generalizations of superdense coding to larger "
"systems are always possible, provided that we replace the Bell states with "
"any orthonormal basis of purifications of the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga boleh simpulkan bahawa generalisasi pengekodan suprapadat kepada "
"sistem yang lebih besar sentiasa mungkin, dengan syarat kita menggantikan "
"keadaan Bell dengan mana-mana asas ortonormal penulenan keadaan bercampur "
"penuh.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Cryptographic implications {#cryptographic-implications}"
msgstr "Implikasi kriptografi {#cryptographic-implications}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The unitary equivalence of purifications has implications concerning the implementation of cryptographic primitives using quantum information.\n"
"For instance, the unitary equivalence of purifications reveals that it is impossible to implement an ideal form of *bit commitment* using quantum information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kesetaraan unitari penulenan mempunyai implikasi berkaitan pelaksanaan primitif kriptografi menggunakan maklumat kuantum.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, kesetaraan unitari penulenan mendedahkan bahawa adalah mustahil untuk melaksanakan bentuk ideal *komitmen bit* menggunakan maklumat kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bit commitment primitive involves two participants, Alice and Bob (who don't trust one another), and has two phases.\n"
"- The first phase is the *commit* phase, through which Alice commits to a binary value $b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
"This commitment must be *binding*, which means that Alice cannot change her mind, as well as *concealing*, which means that Bob can't tell which value Alice has committed to.\n"
"- The second phase is the *reveal* phase, in which the bit committed by Alice becomes known to Bob, who should then be convinced that it was truly the committed value that was revealed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primitif komitmen bit melibatkan dua peserta, Alice dan Bob (yang tidak mempercayai satu sama lain), dan mempunyai dua fasa.\n"
"- Fasa pertama ialah fasa *komit*, di mana Alice berkomit kepada nilai binari $b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
"Komitmen ini mestilah *mengikat*, bermakna Alice tidak boleh menukar fikirannya, serta *menyembunyikan*, bermakna Bob tidak boleh tahu nilai yang Alice telah komit.\n"
"- Fasa kedua ialah fasa *dedah*, di mana bit yang dikomit Alice menjadi diketahui oleh Bob, yang sepatutnya kemudiannya yakin bahawa itu memang nilai yang dikomit yang didedahkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In intuitive, operational terms, the first phase of bit commitment should function as if Alice writes a binary value on a piece of paper, locks the paper inside of a safe, and gives the safe to Bob while keeping the key for herself.\n"
"Alice has committed to the binary value written on the paper because the safe is in Bob's possession (so it's binding), but because Bob can't open the safe he can't tell which value Alice committed to (so it's concealing).\n"
"The second phase should work as if Alice hands the key to the safe to Bob, so that he can open the safe to reveal the value to which Alice committed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam istilah operasi yang intuitif, fasa pertama komitmen bit sepatutnya berfungsi seolah-olah Alice menulis nilai binari pada sekeping kertas, mengunci kertas itu di dalam peti besi, dan memberikan peti besi itu kepada Bob sambil menyimpan kunci untuk dirinya sendiri.\n"
"Alice telah berkomit kepada nilai binari yang tertulis pada kertas itu kerana peti besi berada dalam milikan Bob (jadi ia mengikat), tetapi kerana Bob tidak boleh membuka peti besi itu dia tidak boleh tahu nilai yang Alice komit (jadi ia menyembunyikan).\n"
"Fasa kedua sepatutnya berfungsi seolah-olah Alice menyerahkan kunci peti besi kepada Bob, supaya dia boleh membuka peti besi untuk mendedahkan nilai yang Alice komit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As it turns out, it is impossible to implement a perfect bit commitment protocol by means of quantum information alone, for this contradicts the unitary equivalence of purifications.\n"
"Here is a high-level summary of an argument that establishes this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ternyata, adalah mustahil untuk melaksanakan protokol komitmen bit yang sempurna melalui maklumat kuantum sahaja, kerana ini bercanggah dengan kesetaraan unitari penulenan.\n"
"Berikut adalah ringkasan peringkat tinggi bagi hujah yang menetapkan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To begin, we can assume Alice and Bob only perform unitary operations or introduce new initialized systems as the protocol is executed.\n"
"The fact that every channel has a Stinespring representation allows us to make this assumption.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk bermula, kita boleh andaikan Alice dan Bob hanya melakukan operasi unitari atau memperkenalkan sistem yang diinisialisasi baru semasa protokol dijalankan.\n"
"Fakta bahawa setiap saluran mempunyai perwakilan Stinespring membolehkan kita membuat andaian ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the end of the commit phase of the protocol, Bob holds in his possession some compound system that must be in one of two quantum states: $\\rho_0$ if Alice committed to the value $0$ and $\\rho_1$ if Alice committed to the value $1.$\n"
"In order for the protocol to be perfectly concealing, Bob should not be able to tell the difference between these two states — so it must be that $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1.$\n"
"(Otherwise there would be a measurement that discriminates these states probabilistically.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Di penghujung fasa komit protokol, Bob mempunyai dalam miliknya beberapa sistem kompaun yang mesti berada dalam salah satu daripada dua keadaan kuantum: $\\rho_0$ jika Alice komit kepada nilai $0$ dan $\\rho_1$ jika Alice komit kepada nilai $1.$\n"
"Untuk protokol menjadi sempurna menyembunyikan, Bob tidak sepatutnya dapat membezakan antara dua keadaan ini — jadi mestilah $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1.$\n"
"(Jika tidak, akan ada pengukuran yang dapat membezakan keadaan ini secara probabilistik.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, because Alice and Bob have only used unitary operations, the state of all of the systems involved in the protocol together after the commit phase must be in a pure state.\n"
"In particular, suppose that $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ is the pure state of all of the systems involved in the protocol when Alice commits to $0,$ and $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ is the pure state of all of the systems involved in the protocol when Alice commits to $1.$\n"
"If we write $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ to denote Alice and Bob's (possibly compound) systems, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun begitu, kerana Alice dan Bob hanya menggunakan operasi unitari, keadaan semua sistem yang terlibat dalam protokol bersama-sama selepas fasa komit mestilah dalam keadaan tulen.\n"
"Khususnya, andaikan $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ ialah keadaan tulen semua sistem yang terlibat dalam protokol apabila Alice komit kepada $0,$ dan $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ ialah keadaan tulen semua sistem yang terlibat dalam protokol apabila Alice komit kepada $1.$\n"
"Jika kita tulis $\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{B}$ untuk menandakan sistem (mungkin kompaun) Alice dan Bob, maka\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_0 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle\\langle\\psi_0\\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\rho_1 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\langle\\psi_1\\vert).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_0 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle\\langle\\psi_0\\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\rho_1 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\langle\\psi_1\\vert).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the requirement that $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1$ for a perfectly concealing "
"protocol, we find that $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ "
"are purifications of the same state — and so, by the unitary equivalence of "
"purifications, there must exist a unitary operation $U$ on $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"alone such that\n"
msgstr ""
"Memandangkan keperluan bahawa $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1$ untuk protokol yang "
"sempurna menyembunyikan, kita dapati bahawa $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ dan "
"$\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ ialah penulenan keadaan yang sama — jadi, melalui "
"kesetaraan unitari penulenan, mesti terdapat operasi unitari $U$ pada "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ sahaja sedemikian rupa bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(U\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}})\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle = \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(U\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}})\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle = \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice is therefore free to change her commitment from $0$ to $1$ by applying $U$ to $\\mathsf{A},$\n"
"or from $1$ to $0$ by applying $U^{\\dagger},$ and so the hypothetical protocol being considered completely fails to be binding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh itu Alice bebas untuk menukar komitmennya dari $0$ kepada $1$ dengan menerapkan $U$ pada $\\mathsf{A},$\n"
"atau dari $1$ kepada $0$ dengan menerapkan $U^{\\dagger},$ jadi protokol hipotetikal yang sedang dipertimbangkan itu sama sekali gagal untuk menjadi mengikat.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters theorem {#hughston-jozsa-wootters-theorem}"
msgstr "Teorem Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters {#hughston-jozsa-wootters-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last implication of the unitary equivalence of purifications that we'll discuss in this portion of the lesson is the following theorem known as the Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters theorem.\n"
"(This is, in fact, a slightly simplified statement of the theorem known by this name.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Implikasi terakhir kesetaraan unitari penulenan yang akan kita bincangkan dalam bahagian pelajaran ini ialah teorem berikut yang dikenali sebagai teorem Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters.\n"
"(Ini sebenarnya adalah pernyataan yang sedikit dipermudahkan daripada teorem yang dikenali dengan nama ini.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters: Let $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ be systems and let $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ be a quantum state vector of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Also let $N$ be an arbitrary positive integer, let $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{N-1})$ be a probability vector, and let $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ be quantum state vectors representing states of $\\mathsf{X}$ such that\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert\\bigr) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"There exists a (general) measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ on $\\mathsf{Y}$ such that the following two statements are true when this measurement is performed on $\\mathsf{Y}$ when $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is in the state $\\vert\\phi\\rangle:$\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teorem\">\n"
"Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters: Biarkan $\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ menjadi sistem dan biarkan $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ menjadi vektor keadaan kuantum bagi pasangan $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Juga biarkan $N$ menjadi integer positif yang sewenang-wenangnya, biarkan $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{N-1})$ menjadi vektor kebarangkalian, dan biarkan $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ menjadi vektor keadaan kuantum yang mewakili keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ sedemikian rupa bahawa\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert\\bigr) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"Terdapat pengukuran (umum) $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ pada $\\mathsf{Y}$ sedemikian rupa bahawa dua pernyataan berikut adalah benar apabila pengukuran ini dilakukan pada $\\mathsf{Y}$ apabila $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ berada dalam keadaan $\\vert\\phi\\rangle:$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$ appears with probability"
" $p_a$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap hasil pengukuran $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$ muncul dengan "
"kebarangkalian $p_a$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2. Conditioned on obtaining the measurement outcome $a,$ the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"2. Bersyarat pada memperoleh hasil pengukuran $a,$ keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ menjadi $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this theorem says that as long as we have a pure state of two systems, then for *any* way of thinking about the reduced state of the first system as a convex combination of pure states, there is a measurement of the second system that effectively makes this way of thinking about the first system a reality.\n"
"Notice that the number $N$ is not necessarily bounded by the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ or $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"For instance, it could be that $N = 1,000,000$ while $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara intuitif, teorem ini menyatakan bahawa selagi kita mempunyai keadaan tulen dua sistem, maka untuk *sebarang* cara memikirkan keadaan terturun sistem pertama sebagai kombinasi cembung keadaan tulen, terdapat pengukuran sistem kedua yang secara efektif menjadikan cara berfikir ini tentang sistem pertama satu kenyataan.\n"
"Perhatikan bahawa nombor $N$ tidak semestinya dibatasi oleh bilangan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$ atau $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Sebagai contoh, mungkin $N = 1{,}000{,}000$ sementara $\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ adalah qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We shall prove this theorem using the unitary equivalence of purifications, beginning with the introduction of a new system $\\mathsf{Z}$ whose classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"Consider the following two quantum state vectors of the triple $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan buktikan teorem ini menggunakan kesetaraan unitari penulenan, bermula dengan pengenalan sistem baru $\\mathsf{Z}$ yang set keadaan klasiknya ialah $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"Pertimbangkan dua vektor keadaan kuantum berikut bagi triple $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z}).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle & = \\vert\\phi\\rangle_{\\mathsf{XY}}\\otimes\\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle & = \\vert\\phi\\rangle_{\\mathsf{XY}}\\otimes\\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first vector $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ is simply the given quantum state vector $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ tensored with $\\vert 0\\rangle$ for the new system $\\mathsf{Z}.$\n"
"For the second vector $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle,$ we essentially have a quantum state vector that would make the theorem trivial — at least if $\\mathsf{Y}$ were replaced by $\\mathsf{Z}$ — because a standard basis measurement performed on $\\mathsf{Z}$ clearly yields each outcome $a$ with probability $p_a,$ and conditioned on obtaining this outcome the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Vektor pertama $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ adalah sekadar vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ yang diberikan, ditensor dengan $\\vert 0\\rangle$ untuk sistem baru $\\mathsf{Z}.$\n"
"Untuk vektor kedua $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle,$ kita pada dasarnya mempunyai vektor keadaan kuantum yang akan menjadikan teorem ini trivial — sekurang-kurangnya jika $\\mathsf{Y}$ digantikan dengan $\\mathsf{Z}$ — kerana pengukuran asas standard yang dilakukan pada $\\mathsf{Z}$ jelas menghasilkan setiap hasil $a$ dengan kebarangkalian $p_a,$ dan bersyarat pada mendapatkan hasil ini keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ menjadi $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By thinking about the pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ as a single, compound"
" system that can be traced out to leave $\\mathsf{X},$ we find that we have "
"identified two different purifications of the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan memikirkan pasangan $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ sebagai sistem "
"kompaun tunggal yang boleh disurih keluar untuk meninggalkan $\\mathsf{X},$ "
"kita dapati bahawa kita telah mengenal pasti dua penulenan berbeza bagi "
"keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Specifically, for the first one we have\n"
msgstr "Khususnya, untuk yang pertama kita ada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_0\\vert)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert) = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_0\\vert)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert) = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and for the second one we have\n"
msgstr "dan untuk yang kedua kita ada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_1\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\rho.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_1\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\rho.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There must therefore exist a unitary operation $U$ on "
"$(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ satisfying\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh itu mesti terdapat operasi unitari $U$ pada $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$"
" yang memenuhi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle = \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle = \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "by the unitary equivalence of purifications.\n"
msgstr "melalui kesetaraan unitari penulenan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using this unitary operation $U,$ we can implement a measurement that satisfies the requirements of the theorem as the following diagram illustrates.\n"
"In words, we introduce the new system $\\mathsf{Z}$ initialized to the $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state, apply $U$ to $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z}),$ which transforms the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ from $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ into $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle,$ and then measure $\\mathsf{Z}$ with a standard basis measurement, which we've already observed gives the desired behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan operasi unitari $U$ ini, kita boleh melaksanakan pengukuran yang memenuhi keperluan teorem seperti yang digambarkan oleh rajah berikut.\n"
"Dengan kata-kata, kita memperkenalkan sistem baru $\\mathsf{Z}$ yang diinisialisasi kepada keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle,$ menerapkan $U$ pada $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z}),$ yang mengubah keadaan $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ dari $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ kepada $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle,$ dan kemudian mengukur $\\mathsf{Z}$ dengan pengukuran asas standard, yang seperti yang telah kita perhatikan memberikan tingkah laku yang dikehendaki.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A quantum circuit implementation of a measurement for the HSW "
"theorem](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/purifications-and-fidelity/HSW-measurement.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A quantum circuit implementation of a measurement for the HSW "
"theorem](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/purifications-and-fidelity/HSW-measurement.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dotted rectangle in the figure represents an implementation of this "
"measurement, which can be described as a collection of positive semidefinite"
" matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Segi empat bertitik dalam rajah mewakili pelaksanaan pengukuran ini, yang "
"boleh diterangkan sebagai koleksi matriks semidefinit positif "
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert)U (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert)U (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
